wer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-07a8c960-fbd6-58c0-9b4d-29380f121ae1" :answer-field/id #uuid "07a8c960-fbd6-58c0-9b4d-29380f121ae1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-be49dc7b-f0e9-5b31-9471-e7975f0dc5c4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-be49dc7b-f0e9-5b31-9471-e7975f0dc5c4" "answer-6d60191f-8b09-58fc-88dd-c1feb852be39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be49dc7b-f0e9-5b31-9471-e7975f0dc5c4" :answer/id #uuid "be49dc7b-f0e9-5b31-9471-e7975f0dc5c4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "antisymmetric" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d60191f-8b09-58fc-88dd-c1feb852be39" :answer/id #uuid "6d60191f-8b09-58fc-88dd-c1feb852be39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "symmetric" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-83135e57-d72a-5f9f-8787-4bc48f405724" :question/id #uuid "83135e57-d72a-5f9f-8787-4bc48f405724" :question/math-academy-id "q-213472" :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={5,10,15}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(5,5),(5,10),(10,5)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\n \nthe relation is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nOur relation is defined on ${5,10,15}.$ Notice that:\n\n- $(5,10)\\in R$ and $(10,5)\\in R$\n\nThere are no other pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ in the relation. So, for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the relation is  $\\text{symmetric}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7f3e3ed1-e6b0-5edd-bc5c-8babe4b32fe8" "answer-field-315b90b8-3579-537d-b0a8-3d925fb81f19"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7f3e3ed1-e6b0-5edd-bc5c-8babe4b32fe8" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3e3ed1-e6b0-5edd-bc5c-8babe4b32fe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-7060f16c-94d3-573c-ae34-673a8dbf65fa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7060f16c-94d3-573c-ae34-673a8dbf65fa" "answer-f4dc12f8-b5a2-54fc-ad20-19a9a277ced8" "answer-e8b420ea-8607-5349-859b-557962fda19c" "answer-3024eaf7-b4a4-5c0f-8216-9554c9812c01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7060f16c-94d3-573c-ae34-673a8dbf65fa" :answer/id #uuid "7060f16c-94d3-573c-ae34-673a8dbf65fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y,x)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4dc12f8-b5a2-54fc-ad20-19a9a277ced8" :answer/id #uuid "f4dc12f8-b5a2-54fc-ad20-19a9a277ced8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y,x)\\notin R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8b420ea-8607-5349-859b-557962fda19c" :answer/id #uuid "e8b420ea-8607-5349-859b-557962fda19c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3024eaf7-b4a4-5c0f-8216-9554c9812c01" :answer/id #uuid "3024eaf7-b4a4-5c0f-8216-9554c9812c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x\\ne y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-315b90b8-3579-537d-b0a8-3d925fb81f19" :answer-field/id #uuid "315b90b8-3579-537d-b0a8-3d925fb81f19" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-c2e1189f-caa1-573c