a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nOur relation is defined on ${0,1,2}.$ Notice that:\n\n- $(0,1)\\in R$ and $(1,0)\\notin R.$ So, the relation is $\\text{not symmetric}.$\n\n- $(1,2)\\in R$ and $(2,1)\\in R.$ So, the relation is $\\text{not antisymmetric}.$\n\nTherefore, we can conclude that the relation is neither symmetric nor antisymmetric." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-26c5cf80-3b6b-5cba-a5ea-839b485bb546" "answer-field-d284652a-bb13-5c6a-8a1d-ac6cfcb5ff46" "answer-field-2668b4eb-f6f3-5871-bd6d-323617787958" "answer-field-c65e2230-e4b5-5996-a967-71c371a504a0" "answer-field-29bcb877-e94d-5252-871e-9e5d14fc76af" "answer-field-866fa40e-f8d8-5cbe-8724-d6056076907b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-26c5cf80-3b6b-5cba-a5ea-839b485bb546" :answer-field/id #uuid "26c5cf80-3b6b-5cba-a5ea-839b485bb546" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-bd393ed4-6a99-5c18-beae-ea8420490600" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d1a79ee4-f101-5a7d-b273-883951a66175" "answer-bd393ed4-6a99-5c18-beae-ea8420490600"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d1a79ee4-f101-5a7d-b273-883951a66175" :answer/id #uuid "d1a79ee4-f101-5a7d-b273-883951a66175" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd393ed4-6a99-5c18-beae-ea8420490600" :answer/id #uuid "bd393ed4-6a99-5c18-beae-ea8420490600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d284652a-bb13-5c6a-8