/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6af8410-eb76-547a-996a-a74c4d5fa487" :answer/id #uuid "d6af8410-eb76-547a-996a-a74c4d5fa487" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,1)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b5f8f60-0d74-502f-b467-1aea80eb05bf" :answer/id #uuid "9b5f8f60-0d74-502f-b467-1aea80eb05bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,2)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29bcb877-e94d-5252-871e-9e5d14fc76af" :answer-field/id #uuid "29bcb877-e94d-5252-871e-9e5d14fc76af" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-ef6bfe62-3386-59a9-b6f6-17222e43682a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-68f7d904-5751-516d-9aa6-a353819f6ed0" "answer-ef6bfe62-3386-59a9-b6f6-17222e43682a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-68f7d904-5751-516d-9aa6-a353819f6ed0" :answer/id #uuid "68f7d904-5751-516d-9aa6-a353819f6ed0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,0)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef6bfe62-3386-59a9-b6f6-17222e43682a" :answer/id #uuid "ef6bfe62-3386-59a9-b6f6-17222e43682a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,1)\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-866fa40e-f8d8-5cbe-8724-d6056076907b" :answer-field/id #uuid "866fa40e-f8d8-5cbe-8724-d6056076907b" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-79527f35-52e1-5824-aacb-f7f05d663924" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3fa57cd3-55c3-5323-9d08-cb9cdbba1e6a" "answer-79527f35-52e1-5824-aacb-f7f05d663924"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fa57cd3-55c3-5323-9d08-cb9cdbba1e6a" :answer/id #uuid "3fa57cd3-55c3-5323-9d08-cb9cdbba1e6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "antisymmetric" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79527f35-52e1-5824-aacb-f7f05d663924" :answer/id #uuid "79527f35-52e1-5824-aacb-f7f05d663924" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "not antisymmetric" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204267 :question/problem "Consider the following relation defined on the set $A={2,4,8}.$ \n\n$$\nR={(2,2),(2,4),(2,8),(4,2),(8,2)}\n$$\n\nSelect the options that make the following reasoning correct:\n\nSince for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,{{field-1}},\n$$\n\n \nthe relation is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nOur relation is defined on ${2,4,8}.$ Notice that:\n\n- $(2,4)\\in R$ and $(4,2)\\in R$\n\n- $(2,8)\\in R$ and $(8,2)\\in R$\n\nThere are no other pairs of the form $(x,y)$ with $x\\ne y$ in the relation. So, for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the relation is  $\\text{symmetric}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8e51691e-f830-5422-8951-de5df1038574" "answer-field-1b132b3a-9126-5417-89ca-76b0debdd83e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8e51691e-f830-5422-8951-de5df1038574" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e51691e-f830-5422-8951-de5df1038574" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-6575c01f-cf77-5ba8-8141-df609ef60155" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6575c01f-cf77-5ba8-8141-df609ef60155" "answer-ac8bca78-4b7b-5746-9df3-aed03e18c52e" "answer-503d2955-c940-5895-89c