" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4d33078e-31f5-5d13-be81-ae2ef0517eb3" :answer/id #uuid "4d33078e-31f5-5d13-be81-ae2ef0517eb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e1211940-b0ad-599d-8627-f212253240ca" :answer/id #uuid "e1211940-b0ad-599d-8627-f212253240ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204259 :question/problem "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={1,2,3}.$ Given that $R$ is antisymmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the diagonal:\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ |  | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |\n| $3$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pairs $(1,3)$ and $(3,2).$ Since $R$ must be antisymmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(3,1)\\notin R,\\,(2,3)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cells corresponding to these elements must all be $0.$\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ |  | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nWe do not have enough information to determine whether $(1,2)$ is an element of $R.$ \n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $0$ | $?$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n| $3$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-528cc93b-7bc5-5c38-9cfa-8fc725eaffe3" "answer-field-68cbd4ab-4f0d-5b32-b6c7-050e11e324e5" "answer-field-e3a7a11e-96d1-56e0-990f-397d1da4cf12"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-528cc93b-7bc5-5c38-9cfa-8fc725eaffe3" :answer-field/id #uuid "528cc93b-7bc5-5c38-9cfa-8fc725eaffe3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1366d776-b1cf-5d05-ba47-1198ddc13169" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ebc7295-62c6-5e01-8f31-506b5fcd4f82" "answer-ef78d06e-e5ab-5f31-956d-6f8b331e1192" "answer-1366d776-b1cf-5d05-ba47-1198ddc13169"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ebc7295-62c6-5e01-8f31-506b5fcd4f82" :answer/id #uuid "5ebc7295-62c6-5e01-8f31-506b5fcd4f82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef78d06e-e5ab-5f31-956d-6f8b331e1192" :answer/id #uuid "ef78d06e-e5ab-5f31-956d-6f8b331e1192" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1366d776-b1cf-5d05-ba47-1198ddc13169" :answer/id #uuid "1366d776-b1cf-5d05-ba47-1198ddc13169" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-68cbd4ab-4f0d-5b32-b6c7-050e11e324e5" :answer-field/id #uuid "68cbd4ab-4f0d-5b32-b6c7-050e11e324e5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-321a0857-7bb1-57c9-b46c-9dac414aff41" :answer-f