$ that is defined on the set $A={-4,2,8}.$ Given that $R$ is symmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $-4$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |\n| $8$ | {{field-4}} | $1$ | $0$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the diagonal:  \n\n|  | $-4$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $0$ |  | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ |  |  |\n| $8$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pair $(8,2).$ Since $R$ must be symmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(2,8)\\in R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cell corresponding to this element must be equal to $1.$\n\n|  | $-4$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $0$ |  | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ |  | $1$ |\n| $8$ |  | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nAlso, note the following:\n\n- The symmetric relation condition is equivalent to $(x,y)\\notin R⟹(y,x)\\notin R.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n(-4,8)\\notin R⟹(8,-4)\\notin R,\\,\\text{and}\\,(2,-4)\\notin R⟹(-4,2)\\notin R.\n$$\n\n- We do not have enough information to determine whether $(2,2)$ is an element of $R.$\n\nLet's add this information to our table.\n\n|  | $-4$ | $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $?$ | $1$ |\n| $8$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6915c63d-35f9-5f95-8e62-98c1517f8bbc" "answer-field-41f24ffc-7eba-575c-90b8-e448a2dc7f23" "answer-field-cab96c9e-3fef-5f30-9cde-d71dd298f70a" "answer-field-be7ef2ac-b5c0-538d-ba3c-fb2609ff71ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6915c63d-35f9-5f95-8e62-98c1517f8bbc" :answer-field/id #uuid "6915c63d-35f9-5f95-8e62-98c1517f8bbc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" "answer-916eec5c-e0d8-5b2c-8bc9-3a5f5acf6a56" "answer-fdc498a9-fdee-5b9b-b096-cea07571b6a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" :answer/id #uuid "9a1a5e33-077c-5105-bb24-ef1f9aa49813" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-916eec5c-e0d8-5b2c-8bc9-3a5f5acf6a56" :answer/id #uuid "916eec5c-e0d8-5b2c-8bc9-3a5f5acf6a56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdc498a9-fdee-5b9b-b096-cea07571b6a3" :answer/id #uuid "fdc498a9-fdee-5b9b-b096-cea07571b6a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-41f24ffc-7eba-575c-90b8-e448a2dc7f23" :answer-field/id #uuid "41f24ffc-7eba-575c-90b8-e448a2dc7f23" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-2bf4e591-e60b-5f2c-a32d-a8b7ba26375c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c03158e7-b90f-5604-a985-ced43e1f6a0d" "answer-96c2284d-40ee-5b0b-b5bf-e353e6d52e3e" "answer-2bf4e591-e60b-5f2c-a32d-a8b7ba26375c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c03158e7-b90f-5604-a985-ced43e1f6a0d" :answ