wer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6076a4bf-cf0f-5b9b-84cb-dfe4c8ef6f54" :answer/id #uuid "6076a4bf-cf0f-5b9b-84cb-dfe4c8ef6f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56a1a613-c83c-5c0f-a7ae-743fc6e01a76" :answer/id #uuid "56a1a613-c83c-5c0f-a7ae-743fc6e01a76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dc6a0fb2-4f22-51b4-b221-df03547d2d49" :answer/id #uuid "dc6a0fb2-4f22-51b4-b221-df03547d2d49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d692895-cdfb-5939-b4c3-d559da7a492c" :question/id #uuid "4d692895-cdfb-5939-b4c3-d559da7a492c" :question/math-academy-id "q-213498" :question/problem "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={3,6,9}.$ Given that $R$ is antisymmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $9$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ | $1$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the diagonal:\n\n|  | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ |  | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |\n| $9$ |  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pairs $(6,3)$ and $(9,6).$ Since $R$ must be antisymmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(3,6)\\notin R,\\,(6,9)\\notin R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cells corresponding to these elements must all be $0.$\n\n|  | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $9$ |  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nWe do not have enough information to determine whether $(9,3)$ is an element of $R.$ \n\n|  | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $6$ | $1$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n| $9$ | $?$ | $1$ | $1$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6b3157c1-97ae-55f9-b99d-568c2329c41e" "answer-field-def00347-ec7a-5861-99e9-305b03e6f85f" "answer-field-115032cd-5992-5ff7-97ea-0d14f8ac773e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6b3157c1-97ae-55f9-b99d-568c2329c41e" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b3157c1-97ae-55f9-b99d-568c2329c41e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b35cd459-3870-52ee-b096-503cece7131a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b35cd459-3870-52ee-b096-503cece7131a" "answer-6ebb2e93-8022-57a4-9309-f2a0a3c68666" "answer-7ea3d237-2d0b-5481-b345-cf516b83232b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b35cd459-3870-52ee-b096-503cece7131a" :answer/id #uuid "b35cd459-3870-52ee-b096-503cece7131a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ebb2e93-8022-57a4-9309-f2a0a3c68666" :answer/id #uuid "6ebb2e93-8022-57a4-9309-f2a0a3c68666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea3d237-2d0b-5481-b345-cf516b83232b" :answer/id #uuid "7ea3d237-2d0b-5481-b345-cf516b83232b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-def00347-ec7a-5861-99e9-305b03e6f85f" :answer-field/id #uuid "def00347-ec7a-5861-99e9-305b03e6f85f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-6ecc13cf-1913-5af8-ac26-13b5f6a41492" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ecc13cf-1913-5af8-ac26-13b5f6a41492" "answer-26ac2da1-8554-5d1f-9e3f-187bd60e188f" "answer-78ef574b-3a2a-58e7-a1b7-3eb6093b5c92"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ecc13cf-1913-5af8-ac26-13b5f6a41492" :answer/id #uuid "6ecc13cf-1913-5af8-ac26-13b5f6a41492" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-26ac2da1-8554-5d1f-9e3f-187bd60e188f" :answer/id #uuid "26ac2da1-8554-5d1f-9e3f-187bd60e188f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ef574b-3a2a-58e7-a1b7-3eb6093b5c92" :answer/id #uuid "78ef574b-3a2a-58e7-a1b7-3eb6093b5c92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-115032cd-5992-5ff7-97ea-0d14f8ac773e" :answer-field/id #uuid "115032cd-5992-5ff7-97ea-0d14f8ac773e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9df8d568-fa81-59d1-b253-8d8fd1d0a96f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ad93a7b-1be6-5fad-9a14-508b4f04a472" "answer-819b3f6f-52a3-5728-8062-d75fa6c027d4" "answer-9df8d568-fa81-59d1-b253-8d8fd1d0a96f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ad93a7b-1be6-5fad-9a14-508b4f04a472" :answer/id #uuid "8ad93a7b-1be6-5fad-9a14-508b4f04a472" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-819b3f6f-52a3-5728-8062-d75fa6c027d4" :answer/id #uuid "819b3f6f-52a3-5728-8062-d75fa6c027d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9df8d568-fa81-59d1-b253-8d8fd1d0a96f" :answer/id #uuid "9df8d568-fa81-59d1-b253-8d8fd1d0a96f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204260 :question/problem "Consider a relation $R$ that is defined on the set $A={1,2,3}.$ Given that $R$ is symmetric, enter the missing values in the adjacency matrix. \n\n**Note**: If there is not enough information to determine a particular cell's value, then select the question mark $(\\text{?}).$\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $3$ | {{field-3}} | $1$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the following definitions:\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *symmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,⟹\\,(y,x)\\in R.\n$$\n\nIn other words, if a pair $(x,y)$ belongs to a symmetric relation, then the pair $(y,x)$ should also be in the relation.\n\n- A binary relation $R,$ defined on a set $A,$ is *antisymmetric* if for all $x,y\\in A,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\,\\text{and}\\,(y,x)\\in R\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nIn other words, only one of the pairs, either $(x,y)$ or $(y,x),$ can be in an antisymmetric relation. Note that this condition allows pairs of the form $(x,x).$\n\nWe are given elements of the adjacency matrix in the following highlighted cells outside the diagonal:  \n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ |  | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |\n| $3$ |  | $1$ |  |\n\nAs a result, the relation contains the pairs $(1,3)$ and $(3,2).$ Since $R$ must be symmetric, we require \n\n$$\n(3,1)\\in R,\\,(2,3)\\in R.\n$$\n\nSo, the cells corresponding to these elements must all equal $1.$\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ |  | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $1$ |  |\n\nAlso, note the following:\n\n- The symmetric relation condition is equivalent to $(x,y)\\notin R⟹(y,x)\\notin R.$ Therefore, $(2,1)\\notin R$ implies $(1,2)\\notin R.$\n\n- We do not have enough information to determine whether $(3,3)$ is an element of $R.$\n\nLet's add this information to our table.\n\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $3$ | $1$ | $1$ | $?$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f999aae1-a9f0-58f9-8bee-410f830f1fb6" "answer-field-28b1826a-f40a-5dda-9e62-aca68804c4c1" "answer-field-3e6ff00c-2fde-5b50-89a9-546df0ea1a9f" "answer-field-82c3972f-b893-5c4b-ae16-71b11964817d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f999aae1-a9f0-58f9-8bee-410f830f1fb6" :answer-field/id #uuid "f999aae1-a9f0-58f9-8bee-410f830f1fb6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b70f01d1-c9cb-5c50-9266-5b397436034a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b70f01d1-c9cb-5c50-9266-5b397436034a" "answer-03e361b5-5d8f-54c1-8b56-56d87b031bc6" "answer-c9274fec-882e-5216-b987-9c233b78d971"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b70f01d1-c9cb-5c50-9266-5b397436034a" :answer/id #uuid "b70f01d1-c9cb-5c50-9266-5b397436034a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-03e361b5-5d8f-54c1-8b56-56d87b031bc6" :answer/id #uuid "03e361b5-5d8f-54c1-8b56-56d87b031bc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c9274fec-882e-5216-b987-9c233b78d971" :answer/id #uuid "c9274fec-882e-5216-b987-9c233b78d971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\text{?}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-28b1826a-f40a-5dda-9e62-aca68804c4c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "28b1826a-f40a-5dda-9e62-aca68804c4c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-a123e37e-1a98-5dd4-9865-f32a26b3c2c1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-73f92e4c-2327-5d94-94b1-6b3912171a27" "answer-a123e37e-1a98-5dd4-9865-f32a26b3c2c1" "answer-ef626fef-22f6-5946-a9ca-ea0ac454c2